# Supabase backend isolation

- **`lib/db/supabase.ts`** exports `supabaseAdmin` (service role). It must **never** be imported in:
  - Frontend components (React components that run in the browser)
  - Client components (`"use client"`)
  - Any file that is bundled for the client

- **Allowed imports** of `lib/db/supabase` or `supabaseAdmin`:
  - API routes (e.g. `app/api/**/route.ts` or `pages/api/**`)
  - Server-side code (getServerSideProps, server actions, middleware that runs on server)
  - Other server-only services under `lib/services` that are only used from API routes or server code

- Frontend must **not** use any Supabase client. All Supabase access goes through your API routes; the API routes use `supabaseAdmin`.
